  "id": "ss.relic.scar",
  "name": "Scar tissue",
  "description": "A plate of chitin with two old wounds healed shut across it, each held by its own stitches. Healed, not open: the find is what the body keeps *after* a wound, and bleeding would have said the opposite. The stitches are bone against the plate's dark brown so the repairs read as the brightest thing on the object \u2014 the scar is the armour here, and the armour is the point.",
